cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cosmeron in academic or technical work, please cite this repository."
title: "Cosmeron"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vinicios"
    given-names: "Samuel"
    alias: "okarin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/samucaoo1/Cosmeron"
url: "https://github.com/samucaoo1/Cosmeron"
license: "EUPL-1.2"
abstract: >-
  Cosmeron is a modular, header-oriented C11 library for portable systems
  programming, education, experimentation, and reusable low-level components.
  It provides a consistent architecture for algorithms, data structures,
  containers, concurrency, networking, chronometry, random generation,
  mathematics, text and Unicode processing, memory management, bit operations,
  preprocessing, and generic typed APIs.
keywords:
  - C11
  - C library
  - header-only
  - systems programming
  - portable C
  - data structures
  - containers
  - concurrency
  - networking
  - Unicode
  - metaprogramming
  - educational software
